They will be encouraged to engage critically and creatively with a wide range of music and musical
contexts, and reflect on how music is used in the expression of personal and collective identities.

The Subject content is divided into the three components:

• Understanding music
• Performing music
• Composing music.

3.1 Understanding music
The areas of study provide an appropriate focus for students to appraise, develop and demonstrate
an in-depth knowledge and understanding of musical elements, musical context and musical
language. The four areas of study can also provide a rich source of material for your students to
work with when developing performance and composition skills.

There are four areas of study:

1. Western classical tradition 1650–1910
