Synoptic assessment of GCSE Music should require students to:

• develop a broad understanding of the connections between the knowledge, understanding

and skills set out in the specification as a whole

• demonstrate their understanding of the relationships between theory and practice.

4.1 Aims and learning outcomes
Courses based on this specification should encourage students to:

• engage actively in the process of music study
• develop performing skills individually and in groups to communicate musically with fluency
