4.2.3.4 Supervising students

Students must have sufficient direct supervision to ensure that the work submitted can be
confidently authenticated as their own.

You may provide guidance and support to students so that they are clear about the requirements of
the tasks they need to undertake and the marking criteria on which the work will be assessed.

You should encourage students to reflect upon and evaluate their own music, including considering
the success of meeting the brief/intent, during their composition process.
